<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Jian (Qin)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Jian was a general of the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> under King Zheng, the future First Emperor. He conquered Zhao and, after an earlier Qin army had failed, led a force of some 600,000 men against Chu, destroying it in 223 BCE. His victories were central to the unification of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in 221 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wang-jian-qin.jpg" alt="Wang Jian (Qin)" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E7%A7%A6%E5%A4%A7%E5%B0%86%E5%86%9B%E7%8E%8B%E7%BF%A6.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
